course: dictionary
lesson: 5208
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning, and «jar» is a good example. You can tell which meaning is meant by reading the words around it, which is its context. «She put the honey in a jar» is about something you can hold, so jar means a container with a lid.
explain: «The fall jarred his knee.» Here jar is a verb, a doing word. Jarred means shook hard or gave an unpleasant shock. Nobody puts a knee in a container! Ask yourself: does the meaning fit? If you swap in a container and the sentence makes no sense, you know it is the other meaning.
explain: Check the word's part of speech too. Jar can be a noun (a thing) or a verb (an action). In maths, a jar is a container for counting sweets or marbles, and guessing how many are inside is a classic estimating game. In science, a jar keeps a sample or grows a bean.
fact: A jar is a glass or plastic container with a wide top and a lid.
fact: «A jar of jam» means the amount that a jar holds.
fact: To jar means to shake or knock hard, or to give an unpleasant shock.
fact: «Jam jar» and «cookie jar» are phrases where jar is a noun.
fact: Glass jars can break, so carry them carefully.
exercise: «Sam put the honey in a clean jar.» What is a jar in this sentence? | A loud noise from a bus | *A glass or plastic container with a lid | To shake hard | A kind of sweet
exercise: «The fall jarred his knee.» What does jarred mean? | *Shook hard, giving an unpleasant shock | Smelled sweet | Smiled warmly | Filled up with jam
exercise: In «a jar of jam», what does jar mean? | To shake hard | A cookie | A safe lid | *The amount a jar holds
test: «Priya guessed how many sweets were in the jar before she counted them.» What is a jar here? | *A container | A type of jam | To knock hard | A shock
test: «Careful! Glass jars break if you drop them.» What does this sentence tell you? | A jar is a container, and it can break if dropped | Jars never break | A jar is a kind of cake | *Glass jars should be carried carefully
exam: «The bus jarred to a stop, and the jar of marbles rattled on the seat.» Which word is used as a verb? | jar | marbles | *jarred | rattled
</br>
